Why this commit adds an E2E-only command:
A unit test cannot construct the concrete macOS AppHandle<Wry> required by chat_stream because Tauri's Wry event loop must be created on the main thread. The existing isolated desktop E2E harness does run the real Wry application, so its feature-gated command creates a temporary child session, invokes the production chat_stream entry point, proves no persisted session change, no request_start diagnostic, and no ActiveStreams entry, then deletes the fixture. The command is absent from release builds; the MockRuntime test separately covers queue_agent_message with a sentinel inbox and map.
